Jamal,

Thank you for writing the EdSharp program.  I have been using it for about 
two months, and I cannot tell you how much I like it.  Since I am a software 
engineer, I use it much of the day.  It is such a great editor!

I have been an embedded software engineer for about 25 years.  I got used to 
using the VI editor many years ago.  That is the old Unix editor, though it 
is now available on most any platform.  Most of my programming is done under 
Windows these days, so I had been using GVIM for Windows, and sometimes 
still VI for DOS.  This year I decided to move to a more normal editor, so I 
looked into EdSharp.  It really is great!  I still use VI when I need to 
exploit its regular expression capabilities, since I am so familiar with how 
that works.  but now, most of my coding is done with EdSharp.  I still know 
only the EdSharp basics.  I have more to learn.

I did not see that you have asked for any fee or contribution for EdSharp. 
If there is, I would be happy to get you a check.  If instead, EdSharp is a 
labor of love, then at least I am very glad you love doing it!

Many thanks,
Tom Shults

